==English==

===Etymology===
Suggested to be a clipping of ''commodity bag'', a British naval term.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A small [[bag]] used to carry one's personal effects or [[toiletries]] while traveling.
# A [[sailor]]'s small bag to hold [[thread]], [[needle]]s, [[tape]], etc.; a [[housewife]].
#: {{syn|en|sailor's housewife}}
# A [[Girl Guides| Girl Guide's]] bag to [[hold]] [[dish]]es and [[cutlery]], usually made of [[net|mesh]] [[fabric]] or sewn [[dishtowel]].
#: {{syn|en|mess bag|dilly bag|mess kit}}
# {{lb|en|theater}} A bag used to [[hold]] [[costume]] [[piece]]s that do not hang on [[hanger]]s, such as [[sock]]s or [[glove]]s.
# {{lb|en|television}} A [[cameraman]]'s bag containing various small [[tool]]s.

